    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "Does the truck need insurance to transfer title ownership? ",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
     "@type": "Answer",
     "text": "In Texas, insurance is not required to transfer title ownership, but the vehicle must be insured before you can register with the Texas Department of Motor Vehicles (TxDMV)."
    }
   },
   {
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "How much is truck insurance per month in Texas? ",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
     "@type": "Answer",
     "text": "Trucking insurance costs vary depending on a lot of factors like the weight of the truck, estimated travel distance, and type of cargo but the average truck insurance cost in Texas is $12,000 &#8211; $17, 200 per year."
    }
   },
   {
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": "How does truck insurance work? ",
    "acceptedAnswer": {
     "@type": "Answer",
     "text": "Commercial trucking coverage protects trucking drivers and trucking businesses from financial losses due to unexpected accidents, damage to cargo, or liability incurred through different types of coverage like liability insurance, cargo insurance, physical damage insurance, non-trucking liability, workers compensation, uninsured/underinsured motorist coverage etc."
    }
